Algorithm
1. Start.
2. Declare variables heartRate, temperature, and spo2.
3. Display the title of the program.
4. Get the patient's heart rate.
5. Get the patient's body temperature.
6. Get the patient's SpO₂ level.
7. Display all three readings.
8. If heart rate is below 60 or above 100, display “Outside adult resting range”; otherwise, display “Within adult resting range”.
9. If temperature is below 36.0°C or above 37.5°C, display “Outside example screening range”; otherwise, display “Within example screening range”.
10. If SpO₂ is below 95% or above 100%, display “Outside expected range”; otherwise, display “Within expected range”.
11. Display a message that the results are not a medical diagnosis.
12. Stop.
